{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1556875168,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDIxNzY2MDUzNA=="},"target":"bb9e6d63e0bc62689a9f6aa8c93b21b151bd292c5191e9fadddcfbad6978d5eb","message":"This is largely a search and replace operation that @kyleam signed up to do (thanks!). However, there is one aspect in `rev_create` that I would prefer to have changed before/during this RF:\n\n`rev_create --fake-dates` does nothing but a `GitRepo.config.set(\"datalad.fake-dates\", \"true\")` but it has an explicit method argument, and counterparts in `AnnexRepo` and `GitRepo contructors`. I do not care much about the latter, but I would prefer to have fake dates to be configured in the same way that other configuration is applied, i.e.:\n\n```\ndatalad create -c fakedates\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1556875731,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4OTAyODgxMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3379#issuecomment-489028813"},"message":"I just recalled why I left `--fake-dates` in initially, and that is still valid: It affect the initial commit made by `create`. Any config procedure would come in too late. So this aspect can/should be ignored in the RF.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1557205964,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjMyMjk2ODg4Nw=="},"status":2}]}